      "type": "text",
      "text": "Abx in the catarrhal stage help; once paroxysms start they have limited effect but are still given to limit spread. Preferred: erythromycin for 14 days or azithro for 5 days; infants ≤ 6 wks: azithro preferred (erythromycin ↑ risk of infantile hypertrophic pyloric stenosis); ≥ 2 mo and macrolide-intolerant or hypersensitive: TMP-SMX may be substituted."
     }
    ]
